    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2KI 11:4",
        "textualBasisJa": "In the seventh year Jehoiada sent and fetched the captains over hundreds of the Carites and of the guard, and brought them to him into the LORD’s house; and he made a covenant with them, and made a covenant with them in the LORD’s house, and showed them the king’s son."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 11:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "The captains over hundreds did according to all that Jehoiada the priest commanded; and they each took his men, those who were to come in on the Sabbath with those who were to go out on the Sabbath, and came to Jehoiada the priest."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 11:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "Jehoiada the priest commanded the captains of hundreds who were set over the army, and said to them, “Bring her out between the ranks. Kill anyone who follows her with the sword.” For the priest said, “Don’t let her be slain in the LORD’s house.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 11:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "Jehoiada made a covenant between the LORD and the king and the people, that they should be the LORD’s people; also between the king and the people."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 12:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "Jehoash did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes all his days in which Jehoiada the priest instructed him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 12:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then King Jehoash called for Jehoiada the priest, and for the other priests, and said to them, “Why aren’t you repairing the damage to the house? Now therefore take no more money from your treasurers, but deliver it for repair of the damage to the house.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 12:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "But Jehoiada the priest took a chest and bored a hole in its lid, and set it beside the altar, on the right side as one comes into the LORD’s house; and the priests who kept the threshold put all the money that was brought into the LORD’s house into it."
      }
    ],
